    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d855">

                <pb facs="1646" n="1606" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/8–754: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 855<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Egypt (Caffery) to the
                        Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d855-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-08-07T16:00:00+02:00">August 7, 1954—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>179. Reference: Deptel 205.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d855-f2"/> Embassy found
                    opportunity sound out Gohar re current Egyptian position on local commanders
                    agreements today.</p>
                <p>Gohar said he has repeatedly told Israelis situation Gaza Strip unlike Jordan
                    since only fifty kilometers long and they can come to Egyptian checkpost any
                    time and he or other officer can meet them within 15 minutes. Gohar has also
                    repeatedly urged police sub-committee be set up to handle minor questions.</p>
                <p>Gohar said Israelis always refuse any arrangement involving police officers and
                    UN observers and insist that “local commanders” should meet.</p>
                <p>Re Israeli attitude, Gohar said it is on record in minutes of EIMAC that Israelis
                    said “It is better to kill the infiltrator than to hand him over”.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Comment:</hi>Dayan emphasis on direct contact between
                    “officers” believed here to indicate Israeli desire exclude UN observers and
                    avoid practical arrangements at police level.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
